      "problem": "If $\\text{Var}[X]=6,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{3}X].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=\\frac{1}{3}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{3}X] & ={(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
